Relations between unit-cell s-parameters and Fresnel coefficients in SBR

The relations below consider that scan directions in the unit-cell are defined in the following ranges:

 and 

Floquet Ports of the unit-cell have only 2 modes: 1 - TE, 2 - TM.

Single-Sided Case:

The Floquet Port (FP) is supposed to be placed on the top face of the unit-cell.

R_{TE,TE} = S_{FP:1,\ FP:1}



R_{TE,TM} = S_{FP:1,\ FP:2}



R_{TM,TE} = -S_{FP:2,\ FP:1}



R_{TM,TM} = -S_{FP:2,\ FP:2}



\theta_{refl} = \theta_{inc} = \theta_{scan}^{UC}



\phi_{inc} = mod(\phi_{scan}^{UC}+180^{\circ}, 360^{\circ})



\phi_{refl} = \phi_{scan}^{UC}



Double-Sided Case:

The Floquet Ports are supposed to be placed on the top (port TOP) and bottom (port BOT) faces of the unit-cell.
Also, in the equations below, the assumption is that both hemispheres are assigned with the same medium (vacuum).

Independently of the excitation side,

\phi_{inc} = mod(\phi_{scan}^{UC}+180^{\circ}, 360^{\circ})



\phi_{refl} = \phi_{scan}^{UC}



\phi_{tr} = \phi_{scan}^{UC}



Reflections from the top side

R_{TE,TE}^{TOP} = S_{TOP:1,\ TOP:1}



R_{TE,TM}^{TOP} = S_{TOP:1,\ TOP:2}



R_{TM,TE}^{TOP} = -S_{TOP:2,\ TOP:1}



R_{TM,TM}^{TOP} = -S_{TOP:2,\ TOP:2}



\theta_{refl}^{TOP} = \theta_{inc}^{TOP} = \theta_{scan}^{UC}



Reflections from the bottom side

R_{TE,TE}^{BOT} = S_{BOT:1,\ BOT:1}



R_{TE,TM}^{BOT} = -S_{BOT:1,\ BOT:2}



R_{TM,TE}^{BOT} = S_{BOT:2,\ BOT:1}



R_{TM,TM}^{BOT} = -S_{BOT:2,\ BOT:2}



\theta_{refl}^{BOT} = \theta_{inc}^{BOT} = 180^{\circ} - \theta_{scan}^{UC}



Transmission “top  bottom”

T_{TE,TE}^{BOT \leftarrow TOP} = S_{BOT:1,\ TOP:1}



T_{TE,TM}^{BOT \leftarrow TOP} = S_{BOT:1,\ TOP:2}



T_{TM,TE}^{BOT \leftarrow TOP} = S_{BOT:2,\ TOP:1}



T_{TM,TM}^{BOT \leftarrow TOP} = S_{BOT:2,\ TOP:2}



\theta_{tr}^{BOT \leftarrow TOP} = 180^{\circ} - \theta_{scan}^{UC}



Transmission “bottom  top”

T_{TE,TE}^{TOP \leftarrow BOT} = S_{TOP:1,\ BOT:1}



T_{TE,TM}^{TOP \leftarrow BOT} = -S_{TOP:1,\ BOT:2}



T_{TM,TE}^{TOP \leftarrow BOT} = -S_{TOP:2,\ BOT:1}



T_{TM,TM}^{TOP \leftarrow BOT} = S_{TOP:2,\ BOT:2}



\theta_{tr}^{TOP \leftarrow BOT} = \theta_{scan}^{UC}

